update InformativePages set Description='<article>
<h1>Red flag symptoms</h1>
<p>Here are important symptoms to look out for and actions to take.</p>
<p>Although they may have other causes, they might be associated with Lynch Syndrome and may require further investigation.</p>
 
<h2>For women only</h2>
<h2>Symptoms of possible breast cancer</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Lump in breast</strong><br />See GP for possible urgent referral to breast team</li>
<li><strong>Change in shape of breast</strong><br />See GP for possible urgent referral to breast team</li>
<li><strong>Distortion of nipple</strong><br />See GP for possible urgent referral to breast team</li>
<li><strong>Eczema of nipple</strong><br />See GP for possible urgent referral to breast team</li>
<li><strong>Bleeding from nipple</strong><br />See GP for possible urgent referral to colorectal team</li>
</ul>
 
<h2>Symptoms of possible ovarian cancer</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Abdominal distension</strong><br />See GP for possible urgent referral to colorectal team</li>
<li><strong>Abdominal pain or discomfort that is not usual for you</strong><br />See GP for possible urgent referral to colorectal team</li>
<li><strong>Heartburn / Gastro-oesophageal reflux every day for a week Tired all the time</strong><br />Seek advice from GP<br />Seek advice from GP to check blood count</li>
<li><strong>Recurrent headaches, particularly if worse in the morningand associated with nausea</strong><br />Seek advice from GP</li>
<li><strong>Back pain that wakes you up at night not related to heavylifting</strong><br />Seek advice from GP</li>
</ul>
 
<h2>For men only</h2>
<h2>Symptoms of possible Prostate cancer</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>For men  -  Getting up two or more times at night to passurine, unrelated to drinking alcohol</strong><br />Seek advice from GP</li>
</ul>
</article>',UpdatedOn=GETDATE()
where PageCode='RFSF'